# Licensing

Granada Histórica uses separate licenses for software and content.

## Software

Unless a file states otherwise, original source code, build configuration,
scripts, and software tests are licensed under the MIT License. See
`LICENSE-CODE`.

SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT

## Data and documentation

Unless a file states otherwise, original project data and documentation are
licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License.
See `LICENSE-DATA`.

SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-4.0

Suggested attribution:

> Granada Histórica contributors, "Granada Histórica", CC BY 4.0.

## Third-party material

These licenses do not apply to third-party material. Source images, historical
maps, extracts, externally supplied datasets, and other third-party works remain
subject to their own copyright and license terms. Inclusion in a bibliography
or source registry does not grant permission to reproduce the underlying work.

Files containing third-party material must identify their provenance and terms.
Material with unknown or incompatible reuse rights must not be committed to the
public repository.
